// Representative authoritative schema for Core JIT instruction kinds.
//
// Each operand-list macro accepts callbacks for fixed operands, a trailing
// homogeneous variadic range, and a trailing heterogeneous ProgramValue range.
// The ProgramValue range declares whether it belongs to a Snapshot or a side
// exit. Each attribute-list macro accepts one attribute callback. Keeping the
// lists as reusable callbacks lets repeated includers derive indices, accessors,
// traversal, constructors, and metadata from declaration order.
//
// CL_JIT_INSTRUCTION arguments:
//   name, IR levels, result, effect bounds, operand-list, attribute-list
//
// CL_JIT_INSTRUCTION_FAMILY additionally accepts a final subkind-list macro.
// A subkind-list macro accepts a callback followed by callback context and
// invokes the callback once as (subkind name, context...) for every concrete
// instruction kind in declaration order.
//
// Fixed and variadic operand callbacks receive:
//   name, operand class, representation
//
// Attribute callbacks receive:
//   name, attribute class
//
// Result declarations receive:
//   result class, representation, definition kind
//
// Result class and representation are encoded in the upper bits of the
// generated InstructionKind. Definition kind is stored in the compact
// family metadata indexed by the low instruction-family bits.
//
// Every operand is a reference to an instruction result. ProgramValue operands
// additionally require the declared representation. Constants enter ordinary
// dataflow, including Snapshot capture, through Const definitions.
//
// An instruction with indirect operands stores its operand payloads in
// compilation-owned side data and the side-data offset in the final inline
// slot. Its attributes begin at slot zero. A variadic range follows every fixed
// operand, so fixed operands retain kind-constant indices within the indirect
// sequence.

#define CL_JIT_SINGLETON_SUBKINDS(each, family, ...)                          \
    each(family, family, __VA_ARGS__)

#define CL_JIT_Parameter_OPERANDS(fixed, variadic, snapshot_values)
#define CL_JIT_Parameter_ATTRIBUTES(attribute)
CL_JIT_INSTRUCTION(Parameter, CL_JIT_IR_LEVELS(CoreMachine),
                   CL_JIT_RESULT(ProgramValue, TaggedValue, Def),
                   CL_JIT_EFFECT_BOUNDS(None, None),
                   CL_JIT_Parameter_OPERANDS, CL_JIT_Parameter_ATTRIBUTES)
#undef CL_JIT_Parameter_ATTRIBUTES
#undef CL_JIT_Parameter_OPERANDS

